Three things libopenconnect gets wrong that a client cannot work around.

cmd_fd_write: a new handle comes from calloc(), and openconnect_vpninfo_new()
sets cmd_fd to -1 but leaves cmd_fd_write at zero. openconnect_vpninfo_free()
closes both when cmd_fd_write >= 0. So freeing a handle that never called
openconnect_setup_cmd_pipe() closes file descriptor 0: standard input the
first time, and after that whatever the process has since opened as 0. Set
it to -1 with the others, which is what the test in openconnect_vpninfo_free()
and the one in check_cmd_fd() expect.

no_external_auth: unless it is set, every request tells the gateway that this
client can log in by single sign-on and through an external browser, and
there is no function to set it; only the command-line tool does. We support
neither, so set it for every handle and never offer them. This only stops the
offer. What stops a gateway that asks anyway is the build: it leaves out the
external-browser login (no HPKE), and no webview callback is ever set, so a
single sign-on form fails at once.

csd_preurl: for every host-scan <csd> tag in a gateway's reply,
parse_auth_node() copies urlpath with strdup(). urlpath is NULL when the
address being fetched has no path, as "https://<host>" has none, and
strdup(NULL) crashes with glibc and on macOS (Windows' C runtime returns NULL
instead). So one tag from the gateway crashes the client. Copy it only when
there is one: nothing reads csd_preurl, it is only freed.

--- a/library.c
+++ b/library.c
@@ -196,6 +196,8 @@
 	vpninfo->dtls_fd = -1;
 	vpninfo->need_poll_cmd_fd = -1;
 	vpninfo->cmd_fd = -1;
+	vpninfo->cmd_fd_write = -1;
+	vpninfo->no_external_auth = 1;
 	init_pkt_queue(&vpninfo->free_queue);
 	init_pkt_queue(&vpninfo->incoming_queue);
 	init_pkt_queue(&vpninfo->outgoing_queue);
--- a/auth.c
+++ b/auth.c
@@ -492,5 +492,5 @@
 			xmlnode_get_prop(xml_node, "starturl", &vpninfo->csd_starturl);
 			xmlnode_get_prop(xml_node, "waiturl", &vpninfo->csd_waiturl);
-			vpninfo->csd_preurl = strdup(vpninfo->urlpath);
+			vpninfo->csd_preurl = vpninfo->urlpath ? strdup(vpninfo->urlpath) : NULL;
 		}
 	}
